### Page 1 of 4

```text
File No. 14X002
Collateral Assignment of Promissory Note and Mortgage, Page 1
COLLATERAL ASSIGNMENT OF
PROMISSORY NOTE, MORTGAGE, AND GRANITE LOAN DOCUMENTS

This COLLATERAL ASSIGNMENT OF PROMISSORY NOTE, MORTGAGE, AND GRANITE
LOAN DOCUMENTS (this “Assignment”) is made as of the _____ day of _______________,
2014, by the CITY OF CHEYENNE, a Wyoming municipal corporation, whose principal office
and mailing address is located at 2101 O’Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, WY 82001 (the “City”), to
WYOMING BUSINESS COUNCIL (the “Council”), a body corporate organized under the laws of
the State of Wyoming and operating as a state instrumentality operated solely for the pub-
lic benefit, whose principal office and mailing address is located at 214 West 15th Street, Chey-
enne, Wyoming 82001.
A. City has made a loan to Granite Peak Development Limited Partnership, a Wyoming lim-
ited partnership formerly known as Granite Peak Development, LLC, a Wyoming Lim-
ited Liability Company (“Granite”), in the stated principal sum of $3,000,000 (the “Gran-
ite Loan”), as evidenced by a Non-Negotiable Promissory Note dated as of even date
herewith made by Granite and the City and guarantied by Rich Fairservis (the “Guaran-
tor”), all in connection with the project (the “Project”) to construct railways, spurs, and
switching and related facilities to serve the Swan Ranch Rail Park (the “Park”) in Chey-
enne, Wyoming.
B. The City, the Cheyenne-Laramie County Corporation for Economic Development (Chey-
enne Leads), a Wyoming non-profit corporation and statutorily-authorized community
development organization ("LEADS"), and Granite will construct the Project in accord-
ance with an undated Amended and Restated Project Development and Administration
Agreement (the “Development Agreement”) made among them.
C. During construction and afterward during the pendency of the Granite Loan, the City will
own the project improvements pursuant to an Assignment of Ownership of Rail, Ties,
and all Related Rail Equipment installed pursuant to Amended And Restated Project De-
velopment and Administration Agreement dated as of even date herewith (the “Rail
Ownership Assignment”).
D. Pursuant to a Rail Road Right of Way Easement made as of even date herewith and rec-
orded on ______________, 2014, in Book _____ at Page _____ among the Real Estate
Records of the County Clerk for Laramie County, Wyoming (the “Rail Easement Agree-
ment”), made by Swan Ranch, LLC, a Wyoming limited liability company (“Swan”), and
Clear Creek Land Company LLC, a Wyoming limited liability company (“Clear Creek”),
the City will be the owner, for a term of ten (10) years from the date hereof, of a non-
exclusive easement (the “Rail Easement”) for a rail road line and corridor in Parcels 2, 3,
and 4, as described and shown on Exhibits A, B, and C to Schedule 1 hereof, which
schedule and exhibits are incorporated herein by this reference, subject to the rights of
Granite, Swan, CLH, LLC, a Wyoming limited liability company (“CLH”), and any re-
lated entity to an exclusive option to acquire the rail, ties, and all related rail equipment
installed pursuant to the Development Agreement and all of the City’s right, title, and in-
terest in the Rail Easement.
E. The City has entered into a Track Lease Agreement for Rail Facilities Within Swan
Ranch Rail Park, Cheyenne, Wyoming (the “Track Lease Agreement”), with CLH and
Granite under which CLH will lease the City's rail facilities within the Park to serve vari-
ous business enterprises now or to be located within the Park.
```

### Page 2 of 4

```text
File No. 14X002
Collateral Assignment of Promissory Note and Mortgage, Page 2
F. The City has applied for, and been approved by the Council for, a Wyoming Business
Ready Community-Business Committed Loan in the maximum principal sum of Three
Million Dollars ($3,000,000) (the “Loan”), which the Council will disburse to the City as
provided in a Business Ready Community – Business Committed Loan Agreement made
as of even date herewith by the City in favor of the Council (the “Loan Agreement”).
G. The Granite Note is secured, in part, by a Mortgage (the “Mortgage”) upon the lands de-
scribed on Schedule 1 to the Loan Agreement granted to the City by Swan and Clear
Creek, among others, which Mortgage was made as of even date herewith and recorded
on ______________, 2014, in Book _____ at Page _____ among the Real Estate Records
of the County Clerk for Laramie County, Wyoming.
H. The City’s obligations to repay the Loan to the Council is evidenced by a Promissory
Note (the “Note”) of even date herewith made in the maximum principal sum of the
Loan.
I. The Granite Note, the Mortgage, the Rail Ownership Assignment, the Rail Easement
Agreement, the Track Lease Agreement, the Development Agreement, and all other doc-
uments, certificate, instruments, applications, opinions, and other writings evidencing,
securing, executed, or otherwise made or delivered in connection with the Granite Loan
are hereinafter referred to as the “Granite Loan Documents”.

NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the Council agreeing to fund the Loan and oth-
er good and valuable consideration, the receipt of which is hereby acknowledged, and as further
security for the performance of the Obligations (as defined in the Loan Agreement), the City
hereby grants, conveys, transfers, and assigns to the Council all right, title, and interest of the
City in and to the Mortgage, the Granite Note, all of the Granite Loan Documents, the debt and
claims thereby evidenced and/or secured and all of the City’s right, title and interest in and to the
real estate therein described, and benefits under, in and to the Mortgage and/or any of the Granite
Loan Documents.

TO HAVE AND TO HOLD the same with all of the rights, privileges and appurtenances
thereunto belonging unto the Council, its successors and assigns until such time as the Obliga-
tions have been satisfied in full for the purpose of further and collaterally securing same (but not,
however, for the purposes of securing any other obligations to Council, whether now existing or
hereafter arising).

The City and the Council agree that the following terms and conditions shall govern this
Assignment:
1. City’s Rights until Default.  So long as no default shall exist under the Obligations, the City
shall have the right to exercise all of the City’s rights and benefits under, in and to the Gran-
ite Note, the Mortgage, and all other Granite Loan Documents.
2. Council’s Rights in Event of Default.
2.1. Immediately upon the occurrence of a default under the Obligations, and until such de-
fault shall have been cured, as hereinafter defined, the Council is hereby expressly and
irrevocably authorized to assume any or all of City’s rights with respect to the Granite
Note, the Mortgage, and all other Granite Loan Documents without further authoriza-
tion, notice or demand and without the commencement of any action.
```

### Page 3 of 4

```text
File No. 14X002
Collateral Assignment of Promissory Note and Mortgage, Page 3
2.2. The City hereby constitutes and appoints the Council irrevocably, and with full power of
substitution and revocation, the true and lawful attorney, for and in the name, place and
stead of the City, to exercise any and all rights and remedies of the City under the Gran-
ite Note, the Mortgage, and all other Granite Loan Documents.  The City hereby grants
unto said attorney full power and authority to do and perform each and every act what-
soever requisite to be done with respect to the Granite Note, the Mortgage, and all other
Granite Loan Documents, as fully to all intents and purposes, as the City could do if per-
sonally present, hereby ratifying and confirming all that said attorney shall lawfully do
or cause to be done by virtue hereof, provided, however, that any acts or omissions by
the Council after default shall be at the Council’s discretion and shall not be or become
the basis for any liability of the City.
2.3. Acceptance of this Assignment by the Council shall not constitute a satisfaction of all or
any part of the Obligations of the City.
2.4. The rights and powers of the Council hereunder shall continue and remain in full force
and effect until all Obligations are satisfied in full.  Council shall not be liable to City or
anyone claiming under or through City by reason of any act or omission by the City
hereunder.
2.5. A default shall be cured when the City shall have satisfied applicable provisions for cure
in the Note, the Loan Agreement, and all other applicable Loan Documents.
3. Termination.  Upon satisfaction in full of the Obligations, this Assignment shall thereupon be
void and of further no effect and, in that event, upon the City’s request, the Council agrees to
execute and deliver to the City instruments evidencing the termination of this Assignment
and/or release of the Council’s interest in the Granite Note, the Mortgage, and all other Gran-
ite Loan Documents.
4. Notice.  Notice and other communications under this Assignment shall be given in the same
manner provided for in the Note.
5. Miscellaneous.  The provisions of Section 14 of the Loan Agreement and all of the subsec-
tions thereunder are hereby incorporated herein by this reference.
IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the City has caused this instrument to be executed by its
Mayor and attested by its City Clerk, all as of the date first above written.
ATTEST:
CITY OF CHEYENNE

By:

Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk

By:

Richard L. Kaysen, Mayor

Approved as to Form Only:

Assistant Attorney General
```

